Paolo Chiggiato. *Outgassing properties of vacuum materials for particle accelerators*, 2017 CERN Accelerator School contribution; arXiv version 2, 16 June 2020, 47 pages. [Versioned record](https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.07124v2), [complete paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.07124).

Read the entire paper, including measurement methods, adsorption/desorption, diffusion and treatment histories. Derive the gas-load account and test how surface and bulk processes produce different time dependence. Follow a cited primary measurement where an engineering decision depends on a numerical outgassing value.

Metadata and selected introductory, source-mechanism, accumulation-method, residence/distribution, hydrogen-diffusion and surface-limited passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. The measurement discussion identifies background, gauge response and readsorption as limits of a simple pressure-rise inference. An instrument can alter the gas balance it is intended to observe.

This is an authorized public author manuscript. The arXiv distribution licence does not grant general adaptation rights. Retain version and credits; all media remain external. Material-specific reported values need their surface preparation, temperature, exposure and measurement history before reuse.

